  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The creep resistance of the FCC/BCC high-entropy-alloy coating is governed by nanoscale B2-ordered precipitate networks.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "B2-ordered precipitate networks pin dislocations under sustained load.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dislocation pinning by the precipitates raises the Orowan stress required for creep deformation.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting coating is a solution-annealed FCC/BCC high-entropy alloy with negligible precipitate content.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic CoCrFeNiMn is offered as an example of the starting FCC/BCC coating.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aging will induce uniformly distributed, coherent B2-ordered precipitates with sizes of 5–20 nm.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The aging-induced B2 precipitates will occur both within grains and along grain boundaries.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A B2 precipitate volume fraction of 5–10% and the associated interparticle spacing are the structural mediators of creep resistance.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The precipitates impede creep dislocations through Orowan looping.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Orowan looping increases the threshold stress for dislocation motion and slows the steady-state creep rate.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 100 MPa and 700 °C, the aged coating will have a steady-state creep rate at least ten times lower than the solution-annealed baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed precipitate-mediated mechanism operates from 600 to 800 °C and from 50 to 200 MPa.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Above 800 °C, precipitate coarsening may reduce the effectiveness of the creep-resistance mechanism.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Below 600 °C, diffusional creep may dominate.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
